      "title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-26\n\nLocation: North Manchester\n\nPosition:  Assistant Professor of Nursing Department:  Nursing Campus:  Fort Wayne, IN & North Manchester, IN, USA Target Hire Date:  October 2026 Manchester University invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure track, 10-month and a 12-month faculty position as the Assistant Professor of Nursing . These faculty members will play a vital role in shaping the next generation of nurses through excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service.  What You'll Do:   Deliver high-quality instruction in didactic and/or clinical nursing courses. Collaborate with faculty on curriculum development, innovative teaching methods, and student assessment. Serve as a professional role model for nursing students and colleagues. Engage in scholarly activities including discovery, application, integration, and teaching. Publish and present research findings at appropriate venues. Mentor students and colleagues in scholarly endeavors. Advise students and serve as a mentor for peers and student organizations. Actively support student success and preparation for the NCLEX. Participate in departmental and university planning, governance, and committees. Represent the program within the community and professional organizations. What You'll Need:  Master of Science in Nursing (required). Active Indiana RN license (or eligibility). Three years of academic nursing experience at the baccalaureate level preferred. Demonstrated excellence in nursing practice and education. Evidence of scholarship and professional engagement. Strong communication, collaboration, and leadership skills. Why Manchester University?  At MU, we:  Inclusive, Values-Driven Culture – We respect every individual and foster integrity, compassion, and service. Work-Life Balance – Generous paid time off, holidays, and flexible scheduling. Competitive Pay & Benefits – Comprehensive health coverage, retirement contributions, and tuition remission. Professional Growth – Tuition-free classes, development opportunities, and scholarly engagement. Wellness & Perks – Free gym membership, caregiver leave, and employee assistance programs.   For more\ninformation about the position, please review the job descriptions attached to\nthis posting.   To apply , please select the \"Apply\" button to begin the application process and s ubmit a cover letter, curriculum vita/resume, teaching philosophy, and evidence of effective teaching.   Manchester\nUniversity is an equal opportunity employer, and we are committed to respecting\nthe infinite worth of every individual.  We encourage\nindividuals of all backgrounds to apply.",
      "department": ""
