      "title": "Course Developer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-22\n\nLocation: North Manchester\n\nPosition:  Course Developer Department: College of Business Campus:  North Manchester, IN, USA Target Hire Date: August 2026 Do you believe education transforms lives and empowers individuals to make meaningful contributions to their communities? Manchester University is seeking applications for an Adjunct Course Developer  for our undergraduate and graduate-level programs. In this project-based role, you will collaborate with faculty, academic leadership, and instructional design professionals to create engaging online learning experiences that foster student success and reflect Manchester University's mission of educating the whole person. Through innovative course design and a student-centered approach, you will help shape accessible, high-quality educational opportunities that prepare learners to lead with purpose, integrity, and compassion in a changing world.  What You'll Do :  Design and develop online course content aligned with university quality standards. Create learning objectives, instructional materials, assessments, rubrics, and student engagement activities. Build and organize course content within the University's Learning Management System. Ensure course materials meet accessibility, copyright, and academic quality requirements. Collaborate with instructional designers and academic leadership throughout the course development process. Revise and refine course content based on feedback and complete projects within established timelines. What You'll Need :  Master's degree or doctorate in a related discipline, with professional experience and credentials appropriate to the subject area. Experience developing or teaching college-level coursework, preferably in online learning environments. Understanding of instructional design principles and online learning best practices. Strong written communication, organizational, and project management skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and work collaboratively in a team-focused environment. Proficiency with technology, including learning management systems and Microsoft Office applications. Why MU?  At Manchester University, we:  Purpose-Driven Work – Make a lasting impact on students and their futures. Flexible Opportunities – Teach online while maintaining your professional career. Mission & Values Focused – Join a community grounded in learning, faith, service, community, and inclusion. Collaborative Culture – Work alongside dedicated faculty and staff committed to student success. Professional Fulfillment – Share your expertise, mentor emerging professionals, and stay connected to your discipline. For more information about the position, please review the job description attached to this posting.   To apply , please select the \"Apply\" button to begin the application process and s ubmit a cover letter, curriculum vita/resume, evidence of academic course development, and unofficial transcripts of all earned degrees. Manchester University is an equal opportunity employer, and we are committed to respecting the infinite worth of every individual.  We encourage individuals of all backgrounds to apply.",
